# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` rather than `.dockerignore`: the build context is the
# repository root, so a `backend/.dockerignore` would be ignored entirely.
#
# This is an OPTIMISATION, not the safety net. `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` is a
# BuildKit convention — Podman/Buildah and BuildKit-disabled Docker do not read it, and
# fall back to `/.dockerignore` at the context root. That root file is what guarantees
# `node_modules` is excluded on every runtime; this one exists so a BuildKit build can also
# skip the other workspace.
#
# Keep this a SUPERSET of the root file. Anything dropped from here that the root file also
# omits will be silently included under BuildKit.
#
# Paths below are relative to the repository root.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/coverage
planning
scripts/local
frontend/dist
.claude
